				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/scorpion451" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1918720); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1918720&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608563773" alt="Scorpion451" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1918720)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/scorpion451" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1918720); return false;" >Scorpion451</a></span> <span class="odate time_1442629728 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">19 Sep 2015 02:28</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2378127">
									

<p>Don't get me wrong, I love the AWCY. They make for entertaining stories, particularly because they remind me of what the art community occasionally calls &quot;attention whores&quot;- individuals more concerned with themselves and pushing their own agendas than with creating art. Sort of the artistic equivalent of shock jocks and pop stars- to quote the bard, &quot;Full of sound and fury, signifying nothing.&quot; AWCY are without a doubt anartists, but there are very few of them who have created art.</p>
<p>Its also been long established that the anartists of AWCY are only one of many groups of artists who use anomalous effects to produce art, which are fully aware of one another- see <a href="/scp-804">SCP-804</a>, <a href="/scp-1638">SCP-1638</a> and <a href="/scp-1803">SCP-1803</a> for just a few examples of non-AWCY anomalous artists. As the last will demonstrate, I'm not the only one to point out the difference between artists and AWCY's member's. &quot;9, 9, 9&#8230;&quot; indeed.</p>
<p>As for the meaning here, this is something that grew out of personal musings and experiences while mentoring younger artists and writers, as well as looking back at my own continuing journey, and how my perspective has changed and grown over the years. If it incited such anger in you, then I suspect my goal with this piece has been achieved- not in that it enraged you per say, but in that it inspired a deep emotional response and challenged your preconceptions. Its the question that matters, not the answers the characters here suggest.</p>

							</div>

								
					
