				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/scorpion451" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1918720); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1918720&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608563773" alt="Scorpion451" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1918720)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/scorpion451" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1918720); return false;" >Scorpion451</a></span> <span class="odate time_1442629819 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">19 Sep 2015 02:30</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2378128">
									

<p>I'm kind of surprised at learning that some people have a different definition of the anartist thing than I do:</p>
<p>An artist is an artist, no matter the medium. You rarely get someone who is exclusive to a particular artform- a lot of famous musicians play multiple instruments and also paint or write poetry, a lot of sculptors are also known for sketching and writing, ect. Two artists meeting ask if they're artists first, then what media you favor.</p>
<p>To me, anartist has always been a pormanteau of &quot;anarchist&quot; and &quot;artist&quot;- All AWCY members are anomalous artists, and many AWCY members are anartists, but not all anomalous artists are members of AWCY or anartists. Just like all hardcore punk bands are music groups, but not all music groups are hardcore punk bands, and not all punk groups are hardcore punk groups.</p>
<p>Also, yep, monologue, except for a couple of lines in the middle, some of which are only in the guy's imagination.</p>

							</div>

								
